      <div type="clause" n="53">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 53</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="53" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="112" ed="#liebermann"/>XCVII. Gif mon forstolenne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.13-3"/> man befo æt oþrum, ⁊ sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.14-3"/> sio hand oðcwolen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.15-3"/>, sio hine sealde þam men þe hine mon ætbefeng, tieme<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.16-3"/> þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> þone mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.17-2"/> to þæs deadan byrgelse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.18-2"/>, swa oðer fioh<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.19-2"/> swa hit sie, ⁊ cyðe on þam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.20"/> aðe be LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.21"/> hida, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> sio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.22"/> deade hond hine him sealde; þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> hæfð he þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wite afylled mid þy aðe, agife<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.23"/> þam agendfrio þone monnan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="53" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="112" ed="#liebermann"/>XCVII. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.5"/> forstolenne mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.12-2"/> befó æt oðrum, ⁊ sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.7"/> seo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.13-2"/> hond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.5"/> oþcwolen, þe hine salde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.14-2"/> þam men þe hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.15-2"/> ætbefeng, tyme ðonne þone<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.16-2"/> man to þære byrgenne ðæs deadan monnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.5"/>, swa oþer feoh swa (hweðer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.17"/> swa) hit sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.18"/>, ⁊ cyðe on þæm aðe be LX hida, þæt seo deade hond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.5"/> hine him sealde; ðonne hæfð he þæt wíte afylled mid ðy aþe (⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.18"/>) agife ðam agenfrige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.19"/> þone mon.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.5"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="53" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="112" ed="#liebermann"/>Be forstolenes mannes forfenge. Gyf man forstolenne man befo æt oðrum, ⁊ sy seo hand acwolon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.3"/>, ðe hine sealde ðam m<hi rend="italic">en</hi> ðe hine mon ætbefeng, tyme ðonne ðone man to ðæs deadan byrgenne, swa oðer feoh swa hweðer swa hit sy, ⁊ cyðe on ðem aðe be feortig hída, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> seo deade hand hine him sealde; ðonne hæfð he þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wite afylled mid ðu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.4"/> aðe, agyfe ða<hi rend="italic">m</hi> agendfréo ðone man.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="53" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="113" ed="#liebermann"/>Si homo furtiuus intercietur super aliquem, et sit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.11"/> ille mortuus, qui uendidit eum homini, super quem interciatur, aduocet tamen ipsum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.12"/> ad mortui tumulum, sic<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.13"/> aliam pecuniam sicut sit, et iuret per<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.14"/> LX hidas, quod ea mortua manus uendidit ei; et per hoc iusiurandum wita remaneat, et reddatur homo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.15"/> (interciatus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_53.lnote.oe.16"/>) domino suo.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="52–54" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be forstolenes mannes forfenge.] Gif mon forstolenne man befo æt oþrum, ⁊ sie sio hond oðcwolen<ptr type="editorNote" n="19" target="#Ine_53.attnote.fn.19"/>, sio<ptr type="editorNote" n="20" target="#Ine_53.attnote.fn.20"/> hine sealde þam men þe hine mon ætbefeng, tieme þonne þone mon to þæs<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_53.attnote.fn.1"/> deadan<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_53.attnote.fn.2"/> byrgelse<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Ine_53.attnote.fn.3"/>, swa oðer fioh swa hit sie<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Ine_53.attnote.fn.4"/>, ⁊ cyðe on þam aðe be LX<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Ine_53.attnote.fn.5"/> hida, þæt sio deade hond hine him sealde; þonne hæfð he þæt wite afylled mid þy aðe, <ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#Ine_53.attnote.fn.6"/>agife þam agendfrio þone monnan<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#Ine_53.attnote.fn.7"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="56" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="416" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XCVII} Gif mon forstolenne man befo æt oþrum, ⁊ sie hio hond oðcwolen, sio hine sealde þam men þe hine mon ætbefeng, tieme þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> þone mon to þæs deaden byrgelse, swa oþer fioh swa hit sie, ⁊ cyðe on þam aðe be LX hida, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> sio deade hond hine sealde. Þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> hæfð he þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wite afylled mid þy aðe, agife þam agendfrio þone monnan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="113" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn man einen gestohlenen Sklaven<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_53.lnote.de.1"/> bei einem anderen im Anefang fasst<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_53.lnote.de.2"/>, und diejenige [Gewährs]hand<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_53.lnote.de.3"/> verstorben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_53.lnote.de.4"/> ist, welche<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_53.lnote.de.5"/> ihn jenem [anderen] Manne verkauft<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_53.lnote.de.6"/> hatte, bei welchem man ihn gefasst hat, so ziehe [der verklagte Besitzer im Gewährszuge] dann den Sklaven zum Grabe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_53.lnote.de.7"/> des todten [Verkäufers<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_53.lnote.de.8"/>] — ebenso wie andere Fahrhabe, was es (nun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_53.lnote.de.9"/>) sei — und beweise kraft des Eides in Höhe von 60<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_53.lnote.de.10"/> Hiden, dass ihn jene todte [Gewährs]hand ihm verkauft habe; alsdann hat er [zwar] das Strafgeld durch diesen Eid niedergeschlagen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_53.lnote.de.11"/>, gebe [aber<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_53.lnote.de.12"/>] den Sklaven an dessen Eigenthümer zurück.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone seizes a stolen slave by attachment from another, and the [warrantor’s] hand is dead which had sold him to that [other] man from whom he was seized, then let [the accused possessor, in vouching to warranty] take the slave to the grave of the dead [seller] — just as with other movable goods, whatever (now) it may be — and prove by virtue of an oath to the amount of 60 hides that that dead [warrantor’s] hand sold him to him; then he has [indeed] struck down the fine by this oath, [but] let him give the slave back to his owner.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="53" ed="#attenborough"/>If a stolen slave is attached [by the law] in the possession of another, and if the man is dead who has sold him to the man in whose possession he is attached, he shall vouch the dead man’s grave to warranty<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_53.attnote.n.1"/> for the slave—just as for any other property, whatever it may be—and declare in his oath—[which shall be of the value] of sixty hides—that the dead man sold the slave to him; then he shall have freed himself from the fine by the oath, and he shall give back the slave to [his] owner.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="405" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone attaches a stolen slave in the possession of another, and the person is dead who sold him to the man in whose possession he was attached, he is to vouch the grave of the dead man to warranty for the slave, as for other property, whatever it may be, and declare in that oath of [the amount of] 60 hides that the dead man sold him to him. Then with that oath he has done away with the fine; he is to give the slave back to the owner.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="417" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If one catches a stolen person [=slave] in another’s possession, and if the man [<hi rend="italic">hand</hi>] is dead who sold him to that man in whose possession he was caught, then let [the man who currently has the slave] be vouched to warranty at the dead man’s grave – and likewise for whatever other property it might be – and let him declare with an oath [in the value] of sixty hides, that the dead man [<hi rend="italic">hand</hi>] sold it to him. When he has avoided the fine [by means of] the oath, let the owner be given that man.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> ði</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to ði</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">i. s. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">i. s. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sicut <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sicut Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cum LX hidis <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cum LX hidis Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">113</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K; übergeschr. Co</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K; written above Co</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_53.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">112</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
